{"abstract":[{"text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constructive proof. Edges in position order, each coloured through a fan at its end with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex available. At least Δ colours","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete graphs, Petersen), but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ vertices, each found among the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory. For a multigraph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"digraph.undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedyEdgeColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeColoring","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/EdgeColoring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","con